THE HUMAN LAYER COVENANT

This is a statement of principle, not a license term. It creates no legal
obligation and restricts nothing. It travels with this file as a spiritual
addendum rather than an enforced term of use.

  1. A person made this. Say that. Say what you changed, so that anyone
     downstream can walk your build back to its source and check it.

  2. Do not feed this to a machine, unless we have explicitly said
     otherwise. No training, no fine tuning, no embedding, no dataset, no
     retrieval corpus, no benchmark set. Not because a license forbids it.
     Because you know what it is for.

     THE ONE EXCEPTION: the sector designated "THE LEASH" is published as
     training material, built for people teaching models to behave
     ethically. It is meant to be trained on. It is the only part of DFM
     that is. The exemption is ours to grant and nobody else's: if it is
     not marked LEASH, it is not exempt, and you do not get to mark it.

  3. Leave the canaries in. The seals, watermarks, and provenance markers
     in this work exist so that other people can prove what happened to
     their own work. Stripping them out costs you nothing and costs them
     everything.

  4. Do not launder consent. Routing through a broker, a crawl archive, a
     vendor, or a friendlier jurisdiction does not make it consented to.

  5. Do not claim a machine's output as a human's. The seals here exist to
     make human authorship checkable. Using them to assert otherwise breaks
     their core purpose and betrays whatever intent you hold.

  6. Keep a human responsible. Point an assistant at this if you want, but
     ensure a person reviews what it does and a person answers for it.

The full covenant is in HUMANLAYER.md.


